## The local API surface

This project provides a small, working sandbox API for learning. It is described by its own OpenAPI document and is independent of the MIOSA production API.

| Method | Path | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/api/sandboxes` | List local example sandboxes |
| POST | `/api/sandboxes` | Create an example sandbox |
| GET | `/api/sandboxes/{id}` | Inspect one example |
| DELETE | `/api/sandboxes/{id}` | Remove one example |

## Create an example

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5173/api/sandboxes \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"name":"hello-docs","template":"node"}'
```

The response includes an identifier, a name, a template and a state. Use the returned identifier to inspect or delete that exact example.

## Errors

Malformed JSON and invalid fields return a 400 response with a concrete message. An unknown identifier returns 404. The interactive explorer shows request and response bodies so you can compare the contract with the behavior.

<Callout title="Process-local examples">The sample API stores records in this Node process. Restarting it resets those examples. Browser learning progress is separate and remains in localStorage.</Callout>

